 ## Overview
-VGG Loss for Image Patches is a perceptual regularization term that encourages generated image patches to match the high-level feature representations of real image patches using a pre-trained VGG network [S1, unofficial]. Unlike traditional pixel-wise losses, it measures perceptual similarity, but it is highly sensitive to noise in rendered images, which can introduce optimization bias [S2]. It builds on [High-Frequency Aware Loss](7589-high-frequency-aware-loss.md) by operating on specific patch regions rather than the full image.
